      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that finding an appointment can be difficult and cost might be a concern, but ignoring potentially serious symptoms can be risky. Even though stretching and using a foam roller might seem less invasive and easier to access, it's still important to be cautious with your spinal issues. Particularly with nerve involvement, these approaches might only provide temporary relief without addressing the root cause.\n\nYou're looking for relief to sleep, and while controlled twists and a foam roller are generally considered safe for most people, your pain relief plan should be guided by a professional—especially since your symptoms are unusual and painful. In-person guidance can help ensure your safety and might provide you with additional support like proper exercises, adjustments, or other pain-relief techniques.\n\nConsidering your symptoms, it would be wise to avoid self-medicating in this way and instead seek medical advice even if a professional consultation isn't immediately available. Pain and weakness in your foot, in particular, are concerning symptoms that can quickly escalate if not properly managed. There might be other resources available to you such as telemedicine, community health clinics, or walk-in centers that could provide affordable or free advice. Please prioritize getting a professional opinion on your situation before you proceed further to prevent worsening your condition.",
